5) Exchange Hybrid scenarios (hybrid identity + mail flow + auth)

> Hybrid has multiple “boundaries”: user authentication (Entra) vs mail routing (connectors) vs EWS/Autodiscover vs on-prem access. These tests focus on “does CBA break user access to mailbox features in hybrid”.



37. Hybrid user accesses Exchange Online mailbox via OWA with CBA



Expected: Works; no hybrid redirect weirdness.


38. Hybrid user accesses on-prem mailbox (if still on-prem)



Steps: OWA on-prem / published endpoint.

Expected: If auth is on-prem (e.g., AD FS/WAP), Entra CBA may not apply; verify intended auth path.


39. Autodiscover for Outlook (hybrid)



Steps: Configure Outlook profile.

Expected: Autodiscover completes; no repeated prompts.


40. Free/Busy cross-premises



Expected: Works (this is more federation/OAuth config than CBA, but CBA changes can surface issues).


41. EWS access (if used by apps)



Expected: App access works with modern auth; CA policies don’t unintentionally block service principals.


42. SMTP AUTH / legacy protocols disabled



Expected: Confirm legacy is blocked; CBA doesn’t re-enable legacy flows.



---

6) Admin / operational tests (must-have in real CBA rollouts)

43. Break-glass admin account not dependent on CBA



Expected: Emergency account can sign in via alternate method per your policy (highly restricted, monitored).


44. Certificate rollover



Steps: Issue new cert; old still valid; test both.

Expected: Both behave per planned overlap window; no lockout.


45. CRL/OCSP dependency test



Steps: Simulate outage of revocation endpoints (where feasible).

Expected: Matches your documented security stance.


46. Logging & monitoring



Steps: Validate Entra sign-in logs show cert auth; send to Sentinel/Log Analytics.

Expected: Alerts/detections fire (e.g., unusual location with cert auth).


47. Helpdesk runbook test



Steps: User can’t access cert; validate recovery path (temporary access pass, alternate method, re-issuance).

Expected: Recovery works without weakening policy permanently.



